{"diagnosis": "Trace shows loopback send 0xa5 at divider 64 times out with no byte received (FAIL 0xdead). CONE_SLICE has no simpleuart refs (only spiflash.v, system.v), so trace wins. Excerpt shows two faults that together break loopback: line 39 reg [3:1] recv_state is 3-bit and cannot count 0-10 for start+8data+stop so recv_buf_valid never sets, and line 114 send_pattern <= ~1 holds ser_tx=send_pattern[0]=0 in reset instead of idle 1, injecting a false start.",
  "patch_diff": "diff --git a/picosoc/simpleuart.v b/picosoc/simpleuart.v
--- a/picosoc/simpleuart.v
+++ b/picosoc/simpleuart.v
@@ -39,1 +39,1 @@
-	reg [3:1] recv_state;
+	reg [3:0] recv_state;
@@ -114,1 +114,1 @@
-		send_pattern <= ~1;
+		send_pattern <= ~0;",
  "expected": "tohost PASS (byte 0xa5 received, no TRAP: uart timeout)"}

